R1. Implement in Rust as a SINGLE source file that compiles with `rustc --edition 2024`, std only. Output ONLY the Rust source code inside ```rust fences. All listed API items, fields and enum variants must be public; private implementation helpers are allowed. Do not add inner attributes or inner documentation comments.
R2. Use the exact public API below. Store::new() creates an empty store. Error and the result structs must derive Debug, Clone, PartialEq, Eq; Store need not implement those traits. Strings are compared by Rust String ordering, without normalization. Values may be empty; keys may contain any characters except that the empty string is invalid for key-based operations.
Exact API (Rust signatures):
```rust
pub enum Error { KeyEmpty, NameEmpty, NameInvalid { at: usize }, SnapshotLimit, NoTransaction, DepthLimit, SnapshotMissing(String), TimeBackwards { previous: u64, now: u64 }, DeadlineOverflow }
pub struct Store { /* private fields */ }
impl Store {
 pub fn new() -> Self;
 pub fn begin(&mut self, now: u64) -> Result<(), Error>;
 pub fn commit(&mut self, now: u64) -> Result<(), Error>;
 pub fn rollback(&mut self, now: u64) -> Result<(), Error>;
 pub fn set(&mut self, now: u64, key: &str, value: &str, ttl: Option<u64>) -> Result<(), Error>;
 pub fn delete(&mut self, now: u64, key: &str) -> Result<bool, Error>;
 pub fn get(&mut self, now: u64, key: &str) -> Result<Option<String>, Error>;
 pub fn count(&mut self, now: u64, value: &str) -> Result<usize, Error>;
 pub fn depth(&mut self, now: u64) -> Result<usize, Error>;
 pub fn snapshot(&mut self, now: u64, name: &str) -> Result<(), Error>;
 pub fn restore(&mut self, now: u64, name: &str) -> Result<(), Error>;
 pub fn forget(&mut self, now: u64, name: &str) -> Result<(), Error>;
